  "notes": "South has 5 top tricks outside of clubs (1 trick in spades and 2 tricks each in hearts and diamonds). If West has the ♣K, 5 club tricks can be taken by finessing in that suit.\n\nIf East has the ♣K, only 4 tricks will be available in clubs. 4 club tricks will still be enough for the contract, but the defense may be in a position to run the spades. If South wins the opening lead and East has the ♣K, that indeed will happen.\n\nUpon winning the ♣K East will return a spade through South's remaining honour. West will be able to run the entire suit.\n\nThe bidding marks the winning line. West is known to have 6 spades to the ♠A for his opening weak 2 bid. If South allows West to hold the opening lead, the defense is left without recourse. If West continues spades, East will have no spades left upon winning the ♣K.\n\nIf West switches to hearts at trick 2, South can win and play on clubs. East may continue hearts, but South can hold up once. East clears the hearts, but when West wins the ♠A, he will have no hearts to play and South will have his 9 tricks.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
